# Private-data patterns checked by scripts/check-private-data.sh.
#
# This file is COMMITTED and public. It holds only generic *shapes* — never a
# real name, hostname, account number or address. Literals that would themselves
# be a leak go in .private-data-local (gitignored); see .private-data-local.example.
#
# One POSIX extended regex per line. `#` comments and blank lines are ignored.
# A line carrying the marker `private-data-ok` is exempt from every pattern.

# Payment card
# (Visa / Mastercard / Amex, with or without separators)
\b4[0-9]{3}([ -]?[0-9]{4}){3}\b
\b5[1-5][0-9]{2}([ -]?[0-9]{4}){3}\b
\b3[47][0-9]{2}[ -]?[0-9]{6}[ -]?[0-9]{5}\b

# IBAN
\b[A-Z]{2}[0-9]{2}[ ]?[A-Z0-9]{4}([ ]?[A-Z0-9]{4}){2,6}\b

# US Social Security number
\b[0-9]{3}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{4}\b

# Nextcloud app password (five dash-separated groups of five)
\b[a-zA-Z0-9]{5}-[a-zA-Z0-9]{5}-[a-zA-Z0-9]{5}-[a-zA-Z0-9]{5}-[a-zA-Z0-9]{5}\b

# Provider API key
# (only prefixes that are unambiguous on sight)
\bsk-ant-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}
\bsk-or-v1-[a-f0-9]{32,}
\bghp_[A-Za-z0-9]{36}\b
\bglpat-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}\b
